        "original_id": "666862ee-2ccf-5738-ba7c-01ec61ff4259",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Admiral Clarey Bridge, Ford Island, Pearl Harbor, Oahu, Hawaii\n- Organizations: United States Navy\n- Concepts: pontoon bridges, floating bridges, movable spans\n\nFacts:\n- Ford Island is an islet in the center of Pearl Harbor on Oahu in the U.S. state of Hawaii.\n- The United States Navy has an installation on Ford Island.\n- Admiral Clarey Bridge, also known as the Ford Island Bridge, provides access to Ford Island.\n- Admiral Clarey Bridge is a pontoon bridge, commonly described as a floating concrete drawbridge.\n- Admiral Clarey Bridge is one of only a few floating bridges.\n- Admiral Clarey Bridge has the largest floating movable span in the world.",
